#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:0
msgid ""
"Learn how to set up your local environment, build the docs, then test and "
"submit your contributions to snap documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:8
msgid "Local development"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:10
msgid ""
"This page outlines the different ways in which you can contribute to the "
"Snap documentation. Please take the time to become familiar with the "
"contents of this page before you begin contributing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:14
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:16
msgid "**Code of Conduct**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:17
msgid ""
"You will need to read and agree to the Ubuntu [Code of Conduct](https://"
"ubuntu.com/community/docs/ethos/code-of-conduct). By participating, you "
"implicitly agree to abide by the Code of Conduct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:19
msgid "**GitHub account**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:20
msgid ""
"You need a free [GitHub account](https://github.com/) to create issues, "
"comment, reply, or submit contributions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:21
msgid ""
"You don't need to know `git` before you start. For many small contributions, "
"especially where only one page is being changed, you can edit pages directly "
"through GitHub's web interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:23
msgid "Workflow overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:25
msgid "{ref}`Find an issue to work on <finding-issues>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:26
msgid "{ref}`Pick your workflow <choose-workflow>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:27
msgid "{ref}`Test your contribution <doc-testing>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:28
msgid "{ref}`Submit it for review <submit-work>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:31
msgid "Find issues to work on"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:33
msgid ""
"We use GitHub issues to track documentation tasks. Start by [checking our "
"issues list](https://github.com/canonical/snap-docs/issues) to see if there "
"are any tasks you'd like to work on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:37
msgid ""
"You can see which issues are unassigned by selecting \"Assigned to nobody\" "
"from the \"Assignee\" drop-down menu (or [use this link](https://github.com/"
"canonical/snap-docs/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+no%3Aassignee) as a "
"shortcut)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:41
msgid "Claim an issue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:43
msgid ""
"If you find a task you want to work on, leave a comment on the issue to let "
"us know. A maintainer will respond and assign that issue to you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:46
msgid "You can claim one open issue at a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:48
msgid "Create a new issue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:50
msgid ""
"If you have an idea that isn't covered by an existing open issue, create one "
"with an outline of what you want to do. A maintainer will review your idea "
"and either:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:53
msgid ""
"Agree the change is within the project's scope and assign it to you so you "
"can begin working on it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:54
msgid "Discuss and offer suggestions to improve your outline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:55
msgid ""
"Close the issue if it is out of scope of the project or does not meet our "
"contribution guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:58
msgid "Choose your workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:60
msgid ""
"After you have found an issue you want to work on, and have been assigned "
"the issue, you have two options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:63
msgid ""
"**Direct edits via GitHub web interface**: For simple changes like typos or "
"minor corrections using the GitHub web interface, see {ref}`quickstart guide "
"<small-changes-in-gh>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:67
msgid ""
"**Local development**: For more substantial or complex changes, for example "
"to multiple pages, continue with {ref}`local-setup`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:71
msgid "Small changes directly in GitHub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:73
msgid ""
"For small and straightforward contributions that don't need local testing, "
"such as typos or minor corrections, it can be easier to edit pages directly "
"through [GitHub's web interface](https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/"
"working-with-files/managing-files/editing-files). This approach is valid "
"whether you are fixing a single typo, or making multiple changes to a single "
"file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:79
msgid ""
"Navigate to the page you want to edit [in the documentation](https://"
"ubuntu.com/server/docs)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:80
msgid ""
"Click the \"Edit on GitHub\" button (pencil icon) at the top of the page "
"(you will be prompted to create a GitHub account if you don't already have "
"one)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:81
msgid "Make your changes in the GitHub web editor and save them"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:82
msgid "Select \"Create a new branch for this commit and start a pull request\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:83
msgid ""
"Fill in the pull request template, including a description of why the change "
"is needed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:84
msgid "Submit the pull request, and you're done!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:87
msgid "Local setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:89
msgid ""
"For more substantial changes, e.g. where you're changing multiple pages, you "
"may prefer to work locally so you can build and test your changes while you "
"work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:92
msgid "Create a fork"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:94
msgid ""
"Create your own fork of the [Snap documentation GitHub repository](https://"
"github.com/canonical/snap-docs)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:96
msgid ""
"If you're not sure what this means or need some help getting started, check "
"out the [working with git](https://documentation.academy/docs/howto/get-"
"started/using_git/) guide from the Open Documentation Academy which walks "
"through the process and explains all this terminology."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:101
msgid ""
"Just remember to change all instances of `open-documentation-academy` in the "
"commands to `snap-docs`!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:104
msgid "Get the documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:106
msgid "In your terminal, clone the Snap documentation repository by running:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:108
msgid "git clone git@github.com:canonical/snap-docs.git\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:112
msgid ""
"This creates a new folder on your machine called `snap-docs` containing the "
"contents of this repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:115
msgid "Navigate to this folder:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:117
msgid "cd snap-docs\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:121
msgid "Create a new branch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:123
msgid ""
"Before making any changes, ensure the `main` branch on your machine is up-to-"
"date with any recent changes made to the remote repository:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:126
msgid "git pull\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:131
msgid ""
"This won't have any effect if you have only just cloned the repository "
"(since you're already up-to-date)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:135
msgid "Now, create a branch and switch to it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:137
msgid "git checkout -b my-new-branch\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:141
msgid ""
"It's a good idea to give your branch a descriptive name (something more "
"useful than `my-new-branch`). Then, even if you are working on multiple "
"branches, you will know at a glance what each of them is for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:145
msgid "Build and preview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:147
msgid ""
"You're now ready to start working on the docs! Run the following command to "
"build a live preview:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:150
msgid "make run\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:154
msgid ""
"This builds **and serves** the documentation at [http://127.0.0.1:8000/]"
"(http://127.0.0.1:8000/). It watches the folder so that whenever you save "
"changes to a file, the page gets rebuilt. In this way, you can see the "
"effect of your changes (or be warned if something got broken!)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:159
msgid ""
"If you are building locally on an Ubuntu Cloud VM or a container, you may "
"experience issues accessing the page from your host's browser. To resolve "
"this, add the export variable to your shell by running the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:163
msgid "export SPHINX_HOST=0.0.0.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:167
msgid "The `make run` command should then work as expected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:170
msgid ""
"If you have problems getting the documentation to run on your machine, reach "
"out to the team or leave a comment on your issue to get additional support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:175
msgid "Other build commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:177
msgid "You can also use these commands for different purposes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:179
msgid "`make html` -- Build the documentation only (without serving)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:180
msgid "`make serve` -- Serve previously built documentation without rebuilding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:181
msgid "`make clean-doc` -- Clean all built files to start fresh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:183
msgid "Run `make` by itself to see a list of all available commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:186
msgid "Test your changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:188
msgid ""
"Once you think you are ready to submit your changes, test the documentation "
"to catch any spelling errors, broken links, or similar issues. This allows "
"reviewers to focus on the main changes you are proposing and makes the "
"review process more efficient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:193
msgid "Manual testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:195
msgid ""
"If your contribution contains any code or process steps, do a final run-"
"through of your guide from start to finish in a clean environment. This "
"ensures everything works as expected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:199
msgid ""
"Particularly check code snippets -- does the output in your terminal match "
"what you've presented in the guide?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:202
msgid "Creating redirects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:204
msgid ""
"If you rename, move or delete an existing file, you *must* create a redirect "
"for that page to ensure users don't run into 404 errors when clicking links "
"in the published documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:208
msgid "Internal redirects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:210
msgid ""
"To set up a redirect from one file path to another, add a line to the end of "
"`redirects.txt` file in the `docs/` directory, in the following format:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:213
msgid "redirect/path/from/ redirect/path/to/\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:217
msgid ""
"Note that since we use `dirhtml` to build, the built documentation is in the "
"format `path/to/file/index.html` where `file` corresponds to the file name "
"you are redirecting. This means that you only need a trailing slash at the "
"end of the file name, without the file extension. See the [Sphinx Rediraffe "
"docs](https://sphinxext-rediraffe.readthedocs.io/en/latest/) for more "
"guidance, or reach out to us for help."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:224
msgid "External redirects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:226
msgid ""
"Rediraffe doesn't currently handle redirects from a page to an external "
"website. To redirect outside of the Server documentation, you will need to "
"set up a redirect in the `conf.py` file in the root directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:230
msgid ""
"Under the Redirects section, add the source page and the target page as "
"follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:232
msgid ""
"redirects = {\n"
"    \"example/source\": \"https://exampletarget.org\",\n"
"    \"how-to/containers/lxc-containers\": \"https://linuxcontainers.org/lxc/"
"documentation/\",\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:239
msgid ""
"When you set up a redirect in this way, the path of the source file you're "
"redirecting from should include everything *after* the base URL (https://"
"ubuntu.com/server/docs)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:244
msgid "Submitting your pull request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:246
msgid ""
"Once you've completed and tested your changes, you're ready to submit them "
"for review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:249
msgid "Commit your changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:251
msgid "Make sure all your proposed changes are committed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:253
msgid "`git status` will show your not-yet committed changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:254
msgid ""
"Select the ones you want to add to each commit using `git add <filename>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:255
msgid "Commit your selected changes using `git commit`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:258
msgid ""
"Try to group your changes logically. For example, if you have one set of "
"changes that modifies spelling in 10 files, and another set of changes that "
"modifies formatting in 10 different files, you can group them into two "
"commits (one for spelling, and one for formatting). You don't need a "
"separate commit for every file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:265
msgid "Push and create a pull request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:267
msgid "Push the changes to your fork:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:269
msgid "git push <your username> <branch name>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:273
msgid ""
"Then [create a pull request](https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/"
"collaborating-with-pull-requests/proposing-changes-to-your-work-with-pull-"
"requests/creating-a-pull-request) against the Snap documentation repository "
"and fill in the pull request template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:277
msgid "Click submit when you're ready!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:279
msgid "Read the Docs preview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:281
msgid ""
"You will be able to see a live preview of your documentation as it will "
"appear on Read the Docs at the bottom of your pull request's page. Where the "
"checks appear, click on \"Show all checks\" and next to the \"docs/"
"readthedocs\" line, click on \"Details\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:286
msgid "Reviews"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:288
msgid ""
"After you have submitted your PR, one of the Snap documentation maintainers "
"will review it. Depending on time zones and where we are in the development "
"cycle, there may be a delay before your PR is reviewed. Please be patient!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:292
msgid ""
"One or more of the Snap team maintainers will review the changes you have "
"proposed, and they will either \"Approve\" the changes, or leave some "
"feedback and suggested changes (with reasons). If you agree with the "
"feedback, you can make the suggested changes, and the reviewer will approve "
"the PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:298
msgid ""
"The team has adopted the [Conventional Comments](https://"
"conventionalcomments.org/) approach with the intention of making feedback "
"easier to parse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:302
msgid ""
"If you disagree with any parts of the review, it's OK to discuss this with "
"the reviewer -- feedback is made in good faith, and is intended to help "
"strengthen your contribution. This is a collaboration, after all! It's quite "
"normal to have some back-and-forth on a PR, but it should be a respectful "
"dialogue on all sides."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/local-development.md:308
msgid ""
"Once the discussion has concluded, and you have made any agreed changes, the "
"PR will be approved and then merged. Congratulations (and thank you)! You "
"are now an open source contributor!"
msgstr ""
